  "title": "Ospreys hone rescue capabilities, combat readiness",
  "description": "A CV-22B Osprey tiltrotor aircraft assigned to the 8th Special Operations Squadron conduct combat readiness and rescue training in northwest Florida, Nov. 16, 2020. Aircrew members with the 8th SOS fired approximately 600 rounds of .50-caliber ammunition and conducted simulated rescue hoists, honing aircrew proficiency to conduct global special operations any time, any place. (U.S. Air Force video by Senior Airman Edward Coddington)",
